==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Sifu Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Shigong Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
An incredibly tanky and spammable Rare unit similar to an anti-Zombie [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Rocker Cat]], Sifu Cat is a wonderful meatshield against his niche, capable of tanking several hits from Zombie bosses such as [[Lord Gravey]], [[Zamelle]], [[Inumusha]] and even [[Daboo of the Dead]], stalling them while also doing decent damage.

The Multi-Hit ability decreases Sifu Cat's overall DPS, as it divides his attack's damage into three hits. As such, Sifu Cat will sometimes impede [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killer units]] from landing the final hit, although this also makes it more likely to trigger in a large group of units. Sifu Cat's somewhat long recharge time when compared to other meatshields, even those with higher stats such as Rocker, makes using him as your only meatshield a poor choice in most stages unless "Research" Effect UP [[Cat Combo|Combo]]s are also used. Additionally, his cost is relatively high for a meatshield, making his usability more limited considering what he does, as while he can tank and dish out decent damage, he requires support from other anti-Zombies against stronger foes like [[Zang Roo]], as he has no hope of taking them out directly.

==='''True Form'''===
Shigong Cat gains a simple health increase and slow immunity. He can now counter Daboo of the Dead and [[Zomboe]] much better, while the health boost further improves his matchup against Zombies. He still keeps his general problems but is even better at what he does and can be an excellent addition in many Zombie stages.

==='''Talents'''===
Shigong's first [[Talents|Talent]] is a 5% chance to Weaken his target to 50%. Being fairly cheap for what it does, this has a major implication on its utility with its rapid attacks, as Weaken can greatly improve its own survivability, and that of other units. However, practicality is generally on the lower side, as Zombie units tend to abuse abilities in order to penetrate your front lines. Use cases can be found when dealing with Dread Bore, Zir Zeal, and Zomboe, but with a low activation rate, it can feel like a waste when it doesn't activate during crucial moments.

Warp Immunity is rather situational. [[Zapy]], the only Zombie with this ability, is notorious for dealing extreme single-target damage, greatly reducing its relevancy. However, this talent is likely to help when doing [[Zombie Outbreaks|Outbreaks]] for [[Cats of the Cosmos]], where zombies are often mixed with Warp attackers and a punishing deployment limit.

Resist freeze isn't particularly useful, as the only zombies that freeze are [[Zir Zeal]], [[Deathshund]] and [[Death Angel Z-Onel]], both of which are better dealt through other means. [[Henry]] however can be a point in its favor if he happens to be supporting Zombie pushers, as his near-perfect uptime will simply allow other threats to advance. Some example stages are [[Virtual Nightmare]] and [[Steamworks Ltd.]]

Lastly, Shigong has the basic stat talents. HP Buff is often preferred to further augment its potential as an anti-Zombie specialist meatshield, but more damage doesn't hurt.

==='''Orb'''===
A Resistant Up or Health Up vs. Zombies orb will work very well for Shigong Cat to further improve his resilience versus his targeted trait.

For ability orbs, Cash Back is a very solid option, just like Ramen Cat to improve his cost-effectiveness. Alternatively the Cat Cannon charge ability orb is also recommended as you can use your anti-Zombie meatshield to charge your Holy Blast, though this orb is better used on [[Li'l Tank Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Eraser Cat]] if available.

